# Track 5 — Dynamic BlueStacks/FF Universal Candidate Bridge — COMPLETE

Date: 2026-09-09
Branch: `build/initial-product`
Application SHA: `39246089fb28f510287e79639356a4e16d1b6b02`
Commit: `feat: bridge dynamic BlueStacks candidates into universal tuning space`
Windows CI: #1014 — SUCCESS
Run id: `34422254555`

## Verified scope

- Added `BlueStacksUniversalTuningCandidateBinding`, preserving an exact one-to-one relation between a neutral `UniversalTuningCandidate` and the existing specialized `TuningCandidate`.
- Added `BlueStacksUniversalTuningCandidateSpace` and pure/read-only `BlueStacksUniversalTuningCandidateBridge`.
- Stable workload identity comes only from `LegacyGameIdentityBridge` and exact `GameAdapterResolver` resolution to the matching `BlueStacksFreeFireGameAdapter` for `FreeFire` or `FreeFireMax`.
- The existing `AutoTunerEngine.GenerateCandidates(EnvironmentSnapshot, BlueStacksInstance?, AutoTunerMode)` remains the only source of the dynamic specialized candidate set.
- The bridge preserves the specialized generator's surviving candidate order and its existing bounded budget; it may filter but never add/reorder/regenerate candidates.
- Applicability remains owned by `BlueStacksAutoTunerRuntime.BuildCandidatePlan(...)` against the caller-supplied captured allow-listed BlueStacks instance settings.
- Generated-but-unrepresentable candidates are absent from the universal binding set.
- Five workload dimensions are projected under the resolved adapter namespace: CPU cores, RAM MB, renderer, FPS target and resolution.
- Dimension values are descriptive marginals of the exact surviving bindings. They are not a license to rebuild a Cartesian product and manufacture combinations absent from the specialized generator.
- Integer values use invariant text; renderer/resolution text stays lossless with the specialized candidate.
- A captured BlueStacks instance prefix is required; missing/mismatched installed snapshot state fails closed to an empty candidate space.
- Renderer correlation is fail closed: when captured `graphics_renderer` / `graphics_engine` proves a renderer different from a generated non-`Auto` candidate, the candidate is rejected because current BlueStacks runtime code does not have verified renderer mutation authority.
- No renderer mutation was added.
- No change was made to `AutoTunerRunCoordinator`, `AutoTunerSessionService`, `BlueStacksAutoTunerRuntime`, profile persistence, five winner roles, Custom Validated authority, typed PresentMon authority, Global Controlled Benchmark Lease, rollback or History.
- No startup discovery/tuning side effect was introduced.

